# Line endings are not a matter of taste here.
#
# Git on Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true by default — GitHub's
# windows runners do — and a Lisp FORMAT string that ends a line with ~
# (the directive that swallows the newline and the indentation after it)
# then meets a CR instead: "error in FORMAT: Unknown directive (character:
# Return)", at compile time, in every one of the ~48 places the codebase
# uses that continuation.  The .sh and .exp suites have the same allergy
# for the same reason.
#
# So: every text file in this repo is LF in the working tree, on every
# platform.  That includes make.ps1 — PowerShell reads LF-only scripts
# without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf
